WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.264
Google calls Gemini 4 Carbon

00:00:02.064 --> 00:00:03.497
its strongest model.

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:05.140
You probably cannot use it

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.054
yet, because cyber defenders get

00:00:06.854 --> 00:00:07.501
it first.

00:00:08.201 --> 00:00:09.843
The reason is exploits.

00:00:09.883 --> 00:00:11.272
On turning a bug into

00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:12.461
a working attack,

00:00:12.261 --> 00:00:14.575
Carbon gained almost thirteen points

00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:16.623
over Google's earlier model, Argon.

00:00:17.173 --> 00:00:18.747
Exploits jumped the most.

00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:20.926
Finding bugs and writing fixes

00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:22.492
gained only a few points.

00:00:22.532 --> 00:00:24.146
A careful lab hands out

00:00:23.946 --> 00:00:25.632
a model like that slowly.

00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:28.205
Carbon also tops an independent

00:00:28.005 --> 00:00:29.825
leaderboard with fifty-nine.

00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:32.029
The next model scores fifty-eight,

00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:32.853
so the lead is a

00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:33.549
single point.

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.411
The caveats matter.

00:00:35.451 --> 00:00:37.005
The cyber scores were run

00:00:36.805 --> 00:00:38.102
with guardrails off.

00:00:38.142 --> 00:00:40.161
Most comparisons are Google's own.

00:00:40.201 --> 00:00:41.900
And rivals still win some

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.685
coding tests.

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:44.962
Argon took about two weeks

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:46.420
to go from gated to public.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.046
Carbon goes first to some

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:49.894
of Google's early-access partners.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.695
No public date is given.

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:54.198
Carbon will launch at Argon's

00:00:53.998 --> 00:00:56.536
introductory price, two dollars in

00:00:56.336 --> 00:00:57.924
and ten dollars out per

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.874
million tokens.

00:00:58.914 --> 00:01:00.299
Later, that doubles.

00:01:00.849 --> 00:01:01.838
In Fairwind?

00:01:01.878 --> 00:01:02.896
Ask if you are in

00:01:02.696 --> 00:01:03.714
the first group.

00:01:03.754 --> 00:01:05.571
On Gemini, use Argon,

00:01:05.371 --> 00:01:06.893
and plan for its price

00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:08.436
doubling December first.

00:01:08.476 --> 00:01:09.767
And patch faster.

00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:12.141
The head start for defenders

00:01:11.941 --> 00:01:13.156
may last only days.

00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:14.505
And the best model in

00:01:14.305 --> 00:01:15.809
the world now comes with

00:01:15.609 --> 00:01:16.656
a waiting list.

00:01:17.206 --> 00:01:18.638
Read the full story,

00:01:18.438 --> 00:01:20.582
with every benchmark and caveat,

00:01:20.382 --> 00:01:21.425
on The Dispatch.

